{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-10843-r4587253","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Fruit Whip","sourcePageId":10843,"sourceRevision":"4587253","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:34:35Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Fruit%20Whip&oldid=4587253","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:54:20.218Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes using cornstarch","Category:Recipes using cream of tartar","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using ground ginger","Category:Recipes using lime juice","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Refrigerated recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e9f63097338606d7b7b10871492d3e0426e7f3ee66dbbf33c68ce565fa316ef2","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Recipes for dessert\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Dessert]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Fruit mixture ===\n*¾ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*4 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|cornstarch]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] each of [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*1 pinch fine-ground [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n*3 [[Cookbook:Egg Yolk|egg yolks]]\n*Juice of 1 small [[Cookbook:Lime|lime]]\n*2 cups fruit nectar (peach, pear, apricot, or tropical fruits)\n\n=== Whipped egg whites ===\n*3 [[Cookbook:Egg White|egg whites]]\n*1 pinch salt\n*1 pinch [[Cookbook:Cream of Tartar|cream of tartar]]\n*3 Tbsp white granulated sugar\n\n==Procedure==\n#In a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]], [[Cookbook:Beating|beat]] together the sugar, cornstarch, salt, ginger, yolks, and lime juice until pale and creamy.\n#Beat in fruit nectar.\n#Bring to a full [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] over medium heat, stirring constantly, especially towards the end.\n#Cool the pan in cold water.\n#Beat egg whites with salt and cream of tartar, sprinkling in the tablespoons of sugar, to form soft peaks.\n#When fruit mixture is lukewarm, gently [[Cookbook:Folding|fold]] in the whipped egg whites.\n#Transfer the mousse into stemmed glasses, and chill in the fridge.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* This dessert is excellent half-frozen.\n* If pear nectar is used, try substituting one drop of peppermint oil for the ginger.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Refrigerated recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lime juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream of tartar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground ginger]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Fruit Whip","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"¾ cup white granulated sugar","sourceText":"¾ cup white granulated sugar","amountText":"¾ cup white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"4 Tbsp cornstarch","sourceText":"4 Tbsp cornstarch","amountText":"4 Tbsp cornstarch","amount":null,"unit":null,"